# 03 — Severity, Verdict Impact, and Reporting

> Topic: Effort caps, unified BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR calibration, finding table format, verdict impact, and role duties (`H9`–`H14`)

<!-- GEN: Why: coder and reviewer share one severity scale, one table format, and one verdict rule so findings translate directly into action without negotiation. Kind: Mandatory. -->

## 1. Effort Levels & Caps (`H10`)

| Effort | When | Dimensions | Cap |
|---|---|---|---|
| `quick` | Code Writer self-check, small non-feature item, docs-only | 1–4 (changed hunks) | 5 findings |
| `standard` | Every feature phase review (`PHASE-01+`) | 1–7 (changed code + direct callers) | 10 findings |
| `deep` | Final phase before close, {{deep_triggers}}, or a phase returned twice | 1–7 (+ callers one level further) | No cap |

When the cap is reached, keep the highest-severity findings and note in the summary line that the cap truncated the list.

