## 3. Finding Row Format & Summary Line (`H11`, `H14`)

Order findings most severe first, `CONFIRMED` before `PLAUSIBLE`:

| ID | Pass | Severity | Confidence | File:line | Problem | Failure scenario / evidence | Fix direction |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `BH-01` | 2 bug-hunt | `BLOCKER` | `CONFIRMED` | `{{example_path}}:42` | One sentence naming the defect | `given … → when … → then …`; traced path or command (`exit 1`); missing test | What must change, not the replacement code |

End with the mandatory summary line:

```text
bug-hunt: 1 CONFIRMED, 1 PLAUSIBLE (effort standard) — dimensions 1-7
bug-hunt: no defect found (effort quick) — dimensions 1-4 on changed hunks
```

Non-defect cleanups go below the table as `NOTE: <path:line> — <cleanup>` for `code-simplification`.

---

## 4. Verdict Impact & Role Responsibilities (`H12`, `H13`)

| Finding Condition | Verdict Impact |
|---|---|
| Any `CONFIRMED` `BLOCKER` or `MAJOR` | Blocks approval (`REQUEST_CHANGES`) |
| Any `PLAUSIBLE` `BLOCKER` | `BLOCKED` until the named evidence is supplied |
| Other `PLAUSIBLE` findings | Non-blocking questions for the Code Writer |
| `MINOR` only / Zero findings | Does not block approval (`APPROVED` when Pass 1 also passes) |

- **Reviewer (`standard` / `deep`):** Runs cold as Pass 2 of `review-workflow`; strictly read-only toward code, tests, and schemas; records findings as `RV-NN`.
- **Code Writer (`quick` self-check):** Runs on the phase diff after targeted checks pass and before `READY_FOR_REVIEW`; writes a failing regression test first for every `CONFIRMED` finding, fixes at the root inside approved scope, and records open `PLAUSIBLE` items plus the `bug-hunt:` summary line in `writer-handoff.md`.

